## Known limits

- Continued playback across a swap works in Chrome but has no unit test.
- The swap has no timeout of its own; Studio's caller (#4499) gives the whole swap 5 s and then does the full reload.
- A video that a scene script changed before boot (for example an inline style set by a tween) never matches its written markup, so it is always rebuilt fresh.
- Overrides re-apply only inside the swapped scenes. An override addressed by word position (`wordIndex`) in a later scene keeps its old target when an edit adds or removes words before it; a fresh load would re-count. Overrides addressed by `wordId` are unaffected.
- A caption colour override reads a word's rest colour from its stylesheet (or a fromTo's start colour). A word whose resting colour a script sets instead (a `gsap.set` or a `tl.set` before it is spoken) is misclassified, and with an active-colour-only override it can show its stylesheet colour before it is spoken; no caption script the repo ships does this.

## What was broken

The preview runtime's picker (`window.__HF_PICKER_API`: `getCandidatesAtPoint`, `pickAtPoint`, `pickManyAtPoint`, and pick mode's hover and click) listed every pickable element under the point, top first, and stopped at eight. It never asked whether an element draws anything there.

- **A see-through layer on top won.** A full-frame captions section, a mask or an empty wrapper became candidate 0, so `pickAtPoint(x, y)` picked something the viewer cannot see. In the fixture film, the captions section covers the whole frame, so a pick anywhere outside the caption line returned that section.
- **Eight such layers pushed the drawn element out of the list.** The cap ran before anything could tell drawn from not drawn, so a caller filtering the list afterwards could not get it back.
- **A shown child of a hidden parent was never offered.** `visibility: hidden` on any ancestor excluded an element, but a child with `visibility: visible` is drawn.

## The fix

`packages/core/src/runtime`:

- **`pickerDrawn.ts`: one drawn-pixels probe per pick.** An element draws at the point if it has any of:
  - a fill or background image (a colour with alpha 0 in any syntax is not a fill);
  - a picture (img, video, canvas, iframe, embed, object);
  - an SVG shape;
  - a border under the point (its band, not the box it frames), or an inset shadow;
  - a displayed `::before`/`::after` with content, paint or a border;
  - shown text whose line boxes, or the leading between two close lines, cover the point.

  Text is measured per line box, so the gap between two words of a title counts as the title's. The rest of a text box does not count. Text counts only for the box that lays it out: an absolutely or fixed positioned descendant is its own box, so its text is not its ancestors'. Text paints with its fill colour or its stroke, so outline text counts and a transparent fill does not. Words at opacity 0 and text that lays out no boxes (an SVG title, fallback content) count for nothing. An outer `<svg>` counts through its shapes or its own paint, not its whole box.
- **Cheap enough for pick mode's hover.** Per pick, each element's nearby text is collected once and shared by every candidate that holds it, so nested wrappers cost nothing extra. Hidden and out-of-flow subtrees are skipped, as is any box too far above or below the pointer for its lines to reach it (three font sizes, or twice its height up to twenty font sizes, whichever is more). An element with no children is never styled, and only glyphs near the pointer's row are kept.
- **`picker.ts`: the candidate list keeps what is drawn, before the cap.** A candidate stays if it draws at the point or holds a candidate that does. So a click on a title still climbs to its card and its section, and the first eight kept are returned.
- **Nothing drawn at the point** (an empty area of a section): the list is what it was before, so clicking a section's empty area still picks its host.
- **Visibility counts only on the element itself.** The runtime hides container clips with `visibility: hidden` so that a child inside its own window can show itself; those shown children were unpickable. `display: none` and opacity still count all the way up.

What an embedder sees: a see-through wrapper is now offered only where something inside it draws, or where nothing draws at all. An index taken from `getCandidatesAtPoint` still picks the same element in `pickAtPoint`.

Known limits:
- A painted `::before`/`::after` counts across its host's whole box. The page exposes no box for a pseudo-element.
- Pictures always count as drawn, including a transparent PNG.
- Text clipped away by an `overflow: hidden` ancestor still counts where its glyphs sit.
- One block holding thousands of child elements close to the pointer (a whole transcript in one paragraph) costs tens of milliseconds per hover.
- A leading gap wider than about ten times the font size of the box holding its lines is not the text's.
- A border's band is found from the element's bounding box, which is right under scale but not under rotation.
- Characters split into absolutely positioned boxes each count where they are, so the gap between two of them is not the title's. The same goes for a card whose only text is an absolutely positioned child with `pointer-events: none`: the card is picked only where it draws itself.
- Text drawn outside its parent's box (moved there by a transform, or overflowing) counts where its own element is hit. It no longer widens its parent's line boxes.

Hover cost, measured in Chromium: the median of 21 `getCandidatesAtPoint(x, y, 1)` calls, the call pick mode makes on each mousemove.

| page | main | this branch |
|---|---|---|
| a 300-word paragraph in a scene, pointer on empty space | 0.1 ms | 0.2 ms |
| the same paragraph split into one element per character | 0.2 ms | 0.3 ms |
| 5000 words in see-through wrappers | 0.6 ms | 0.7 ms |
| a 5000-word see-through captions layer over a title | 0.7 ms | 0.2 ms (picks the title; main picks the layer) |
| 3000 painted particles in see-through wrappers | 0.7 ms | 1.1 ms |

