## What

Studio's preview now reloads only when a file it actually loaded changes. Notes, reports, logs and editor temp files that the film never loads stop restarting the preview, with no configuration. This replaces `preview.watchIgnore` from #4553, which has not shipped in a release yet.

- The server records every project file the preview uses:
  - the files the bundler reads or looks for while building the document (a new internal `onRead` option on the core bundler);
  - every project file the built document names, before a host rewrites it (so a GIF the CLI turns into a webm still counts);
  - every asset the page requests, including 404s;
  - each sub-composition document, with the root it takes its head from.
- Studio's own `.hyperframes` manifests and `hyperframes.json` are recorded on every build, so they always count.
- Each read is walked the way the system resolves it, recording every symlink it passes and the file it lands on, again on every read. So an edit to a link's target, retargeting any link on the way, or creating a missing target reloads. Projects are matched by their real folder, so hosts that name one project through different links agree.
- A folder event counts when any of those files is inside the folder. On Linux, moving a populated folder into the project, or removing one, reports only the folder's path.
- Both Studio hosts, the CLI server and the Vite dev server, now send every file-change event with `affectsPreview`. It is false for a file the preview never loaded; `affectedCompositions` is then empty, so no thumbnails refresh either.
- Studio skips only the preview reload when `affectsPreview` is false. The file tree still refreshes, so a report an agent writes appears in the tree. Such a change also no longer displaces a film change waiting behind a save, so the film change's editor refresh and thumbnails still run. With `watchIgnore` the event was dropped and the file stayed hidden until a reload.
- Until this server process has built the project's preview, every change counts, as before. That covers a restart under an open tab and a page served from the saved preview copy or a 304.

## Removed

- The `preview.watchIgnore` key: its helper, the CLI config field, the schema entry and the troubleshooting section. A `hyperframes.json` that still has the key is simply not read for it.
- The atomic-save temp-name filter: temp files are never loaded, so they no longer reload.
- Two unreferenced evidence videos under `docs/images/preview-reload-evidence/`.

## Known limits

- An adapter written outside this repo that does not pass the bundler's `onRead` through still gets the document scan and the asset records, but misses reloads for CSS and JS the bundler inlines.
- The set of loaded files only grows until the server restarts, so a file the film stops using still reloads until then: an extra reload, never a missed one.
- "Built" is tracked per project, not per open page, and per server process: two Studio servers sharing one project each keep their own record.
- Hard links are separate names for one file; an edit through a hard link the preview never loaded does not reload.
- The Vite dev server forwards only changes to .html, .css, .js and .json files (unchanged here), so a media edit there never reaches this rule.
- A file the page has not requested yet (a lazy image, media later in the timeline) does not reload the preview. It does not need to: when the page asks for it, it gets the new bytes.

