### Describe the bug

`check`'s runtime warning `gsap_tween_tail` treats GSAP's `force3D` and `autoRound` flags as tweened properties.

`collectTweenRecords` leaves out GSAP's special keys (`NOT_PROPERTIES`: `duration`, `ease`, `overwrite`, `immediateRender`, ...) but not `force3D` or `autoRound`. So `tailBetween` finds a shared "property" in any two overlapping tweens of one element that both pass them, whatever they animate, whenever the earlier one ends up to 0.25 s after the later one.

A composition that passes `force3D: false, autoRound: false` on every tween (ours does, for crisp scaled text) gets a warning for every such pair: about 60 on a 65 s composition, every one naming only `force3D, autoRound`, none a real property.

That hides the case the warning is for. We had two genuine pairs (two tweens of `opacity` on one element at once), found by their frames once 0.8.158's seek drew them in another order, and they were lost among the flag-only warnings.

Measured on 0.8.158 (0.8.152 has the same list). The code is unchanged in v0.8.162: `NOT_PROPERTIES` has neither key ([packages/cli/src/utils/gsapTweenTails.ts, lines 77-113](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/v0.8.162/packages/cli/src/utils/gsapTweenTails.ts#L77-L113)), and `plainProperties` keeps every other key of `vars` ([line 133](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/v0.8.162/packages/cli/src/utils/gsapTweenTails.ts#L133)).

