### Describe the bug

With segmented capture on (`HF_SEGMENTED_CAPTURE=true`, documented in `docs/packages/cli.mdx`, "Segmented capture"), a render on the drawElement path fails at the first frame of one flat colour:

```text
drawElement capture failed at frame 465: suspect small frame (12998B < 20000B); fresh screenshot capture required
```

A flat 1920x1080 frame is a JPEG of about 13 KB, so it is under the 20,000-byte floor. The frame is valid. The one-pass render of the same project, on the same machine and version, meets the same frame. It captures it again, finds the bytes identical, accepts it and completes:

```text
[WARN] [Render] drawElement blank-frame suspect; re-capturing {"frame":465,"bytes":12998,"floor":56346}
[INFO] [Render] drawElement small frame is deterministic; accepted {"frame":465,"bytes":12998}
```

So the two capture loops judge a small frame differently. The segmented one also never makes the "fresh screenshot capture" its message asks for: nothing in the segmented route catches the error, and the render exits 1.

Reproduced on 0.8.152 and 0.8.163 (the latest). The code below is unchanged on `main` (one commit ahead of v0.8.163, which touches none of these files).

**Why, in the code (v0.8.163):**

1. The one pass (single-worker drawElement with worker encode) drains every frame through `createDrainFrameGuard` ([packages/producer/src/services/render/stages/captureStreamingStage.ts, line 320](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/v0.8.163/packages/producer/src/services/render/stages/captureStreamingStage.ts#L320)). It has no floor before 12 frames; after that, the floor is the larger of 20,000 bytes and 12 % of the rolling median. A frame under the floor is captured again with `recaptureDrawElementFrameForVerify`. A byte-identical retry is accepted, and the floor drops to half that frame ([lines 386-408](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/v0.8.163/packages/producer/src/services/render/stages/captureStreamingStage.ts#L386-L408)).
2. The segmented capture's `captureSegmentFrames` captures each frame with `captureFrameToBuffer` ([captureSegmentedStage.ts, lines 192-215 and 276](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/v0.8.163/packages/producer/src/services/render/stages/captureSegmentedStage.ts#L192-L215)). That reaches the serial guard in `captureFrameSurface` ([packages/engine/src/services/frameCapture.ts, lines 4038-4055](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/v0.8.163/packages/engine/src/services/frameCapture.ts#L4038-L4055)). Its floor is `Math.max(20000, median * 0.12)` from the first frame on. It throws `DrawElementCaptureError` on any frame under the floor, with no second capture. Its comment expects the caller to "restart on a fresh screenshot page".
3. No caller in the segmented route does that. `runOneSegment` retries only a lost browser target (`retryAfterTargetLoss`, [captureSegmentedStage.ts, lines 472-515](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/v0.8.163/packages/producer/src/services/render/stages/captureSegmentedStage.ts#L472-L515)). The orchestrator awaits `runCaptureSegmentedStage` with no `try`/`catch` ([renderOrchestrator.ts, lines 4477-4529](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/v0.8.163/packages/producer/src/services/renderOrchestrator.ts#L4477-L4529)). The streaming route has one around `invokeStreaming()`, where `shouldRetryViaPinnedFallback` sends a `DrawElementCaptureError` to a screenshot retry ([line 4634](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/v0.8.163/packages/producer/src/services/renderOrchestrator.ts#L4634)). `replanSegmentedAfterFailure` handles exactly this failure: `draw_element_capture` keeps segmenting and forces screenshots ([capturePlan.ts, lines 220-242](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/v0.8.163/packages/producer/src/services/render/capturePlan.ts#L220-L242)). But no caller reaches it with this error.

The floor sits only in the drawElement branch, so this shows where drawElement is chosen: Windows or macOS with a hardware GPU. Linux takes BeginFrame. Every run on this install also printed "Parallel drawElement capture stays off for this install (a previous render had to fall back)". On an install where the parallel router is on, a render may take another route and never reach this guard; `HF_DE_SINGLE_MIN_FRAMES` and the frame count above keep it on single-worker drawElement here.

