| 0.8.163 | exit 1 at frame 465, `12998B < 20000B` | exit 0, frame 465 accepted as deterministic |

The same happens in a real two-minute composition: a scene that opens on its bare background before its content fades in. That frame was 12,999 bytes; the segmented render failed at it, and the one pass accepted it and two later small frames.

